From: Tobias Fischer <info@tobiasfischer.info>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:52:32 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Load optional heavy dependencies on first use

TagLab imported ultralytics, qhoptim and the CoralNet web stack
(selenium, webdriver-manager, beautifulsoup4, requests) at start-up, so it
did not start unless all of them were installed, although each serves one
optional feature:

- ultralytics (AGPL-3.0): YOLO training only
- qhoptim (PyPI only): the QHAdam optimizer of the DeepLab training only
- selenium, webdriver-manager, bs4, requests: the CoralNet Toolbox only

They are now loaded when the feature is first used. genutils.requirePackage()
imports a package and raises MissingDependency with an install hint if it
is absent; the Train dialog checks ultralytics/qhoptim before it starts and
the CoralNet Toolbox menu entry checks its packages before opening, and
both show the message in a dialog instead of failing at start-up or
half-way through a run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
